# "Exile the top card of your library" with no card in the library does nothing, and nothing is lost for it (a player loses for drawing from an
# empty library, CR 704.5b, not for having none). Bot1's deck is its opening hand, a Forest that Secret Entrance fetches on turn 1 and one Island
# drawn on turn 3, so the library is empty when the Adventurer attacks: Bot2 takes 5, nothing is exiled and the game goes on.

[Bot1 Deck]
Mountain
Mox Ruby
Mox Pearl
Mox Sapphire
Caves of Chaos Adventurer
Island
Island
Forest
Island

[Bot2 Deck]
Forest x15

[Actions]
Bot1.Hand.Mountain.Play
Bot1.Hand.Mox Ruby.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Pearl.Cast
Bot1.Hand.Mox Sapphire.Cast
Bot1.Battlefield.Mountain.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Ruby.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Pearl.Activate
Bot1.Battlefield.Mox Sapphire.Activate
Bot1.Hand.Caves of Chaos Adventurer.Cast
Bot1.Search(Forest)
[T3 Bot1.Upkeep]
Bot1.Modes(Lost Well)
[T3 Bot1.Main1]
Bot1.Attack(Caves of Chaos Adventurer)
[T3 Bot1.Main2]

[Expect]
Turn = 3
Result = InProgress
Bot2.Life = 15
Exile.Count = 0
Bot1.Library.Count = 0
